Claude check your app for every one and build what's missing."}]]}],["$","$L8","folder-method-one-ai-agent",{"href":"/vault/folder-method-one-ai-agent","className":"post","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"cover","children":[["$","img",null,{"src":"/covers/folder-method-one-ai-agent.webp","width":1200,"height":800,"alt":"","loading":"lazy","decoding":"async"}],["$","canvas",null,{"aria-hidden":"true"}]]}],["$","span",null,{"className":"post-meta","children":[["$","b",null,{"children":"Building"}],["$","span",null,{"children":"7 min"}]]}],["$","h3",null,{"className":"post-title","children":"The folder method: one AI agent that survives every model update"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"post-excerpt line-clamp-3","children":"The full guide from the video. Skip the 300 agents. Use the one you already have, give it a map and one folder per job, and write the proof before the playbook, so a new model costs you a few lines instead of a week. Starter folder and all five prompts included."}]]}]]}]]}]
